# Migration rules

- Always follow `docs/AGENTS.md` (injected every session via `.cursor/rules/agents.mdc`).
- Requirements SoT: `docs/Laravel_5.1_to_13_Modernization_Spec.md`. Execution roadmap: `docs/migration-plan.md` (must fully reflect the Spec).
- If the plan would omit or weaken a Spec requirement, the Spec wins — update the plan.
- Preserve business behavior; never silently fix suspected bugs — document, propose, wait.
- Layering: Controller (HTTP only) → Form Request → Policy (`UserRole` match) → Service (workflows) → Model (state + predicates) → Job. See ADR-009, ADR-010, and `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`.
- Models own simple domain predicates; services must not wrap Eloquent/query booleans. Prefer extending the model before adding a service.
- Roles: `App\Enums\UserRole` + `users.role` string column. No Spatie. Policies only for role authorization (no Gates).
- Owner terms/active middleware and policies: owner route groups only — not the shared admin shell.
- Canonical enable flag: `users.active` only. Do not reintroduce `owners.status` as a duplicate. Active access is computed from properties.
- `legacy/` (gitignored) is a **business-behavior reference only** — use it to understand current logic, not to copy L5.1 patterns. Prefer `legacy/` over the XAMPP tree when consulting behavior.
- Original app at `/mnt/e/xampp/htdocs/airconcierge` remains read-only / production SoR until cutover; never edit it as part of this migration; never commit secrets.
- Implement only per Spec, `migration-plan.md`, accepted ADRs, and `docs/AGENTS.md` — those win over anything in `legacy/`.
- Do not port modules or import `migrations_fresh` until that phase/step is approved.
- Phase 0–2.1 implemented (minimal Hostaway per ADR-011); next is Phase 2.2+ per the migration plan.
- No new global helpers; no business logic in Blade; no `env()` outside config.
